# Ze AI Reference
# Generated from code -- always matches this binary.

## CLI Subcommands

  ze [global-flags] <command> [options]

  Modes: [offline] no daemon needed  [daemon] requires running daemon  [setup] one-time setup

  Global flags:
    -d, --debug            Enable debug logging
    -f <file>              Use filesystem directly, bypass blob store
    --plugin <name>        Load plugin before starting (repeatable)
    --mcp <port>           Start MCP server on 127.0.0.1:<port>
    --web <port>           Start web server on 0.0.0.0:<port>
    --web-only             Web UI only, no daemon (config editing only)
    --insecure-web         Disable web auth (forces 127.0.0.1)
    --pprof <addr:port>    Start pprof HTTP server
    -V, --version          Show version

  ze clear          [daemon ] Reset counters, caches, and operational state without changing configuration.
    ze clear help
  ze create         [daemon ] Create new resources.
    ze create help
  ze debug          [daemon ] OSPF debug LSA injection (spec-ospf-ext-14).
    ze debug help
  ze delete         [daemon ] Delete elements from the running configuration.
    ze delete help
  ze fakeas112      [daemon ] Fakeas112 test commands.
    ze fakeas112 help
  ze fakel2tp       [daemon ] Fakel2tp test commands.
    ze fakel2tp help
  ze fakeredist     [daemon ] Fakeredist test commands.
    ze fakeredist help
  ze help           [read-only] Show available commands at this level.
    ze help help
  ze monitor        [read-only] Continuous monitoring commands (Ctrl-C to stop).
    ze monitor help
  ze plugin         [read-only] Configure how events are delivered to your plugin session.
    ze plugin help
  ze request        [daemon ] Commands that act on the running system.
    ze request help
  ze resolve        [read-only] DNS, ASN, PeeringDB, and IRR resolution tools.
    ze resolve help
  ze send           [daemon ] Put an operator-supplied message on a wire.
    ze send help
  ze set            [daemon ] Modify running configuration parameters.
    ze set help
  ze show           [read-only] Read-only commands to inspect system, protocol, and network state.
    ze show help
  ze system         [read-only] Daemon introspection and command dispatch.
    ze system help
  ze update         [daemon ] Pull fresh data from external sources or manage firmware.
    ze update help
  ze appliance      [offline] Manage gokrazy-based Ze appliance images
    assemble, build, clone, config, config-push, export, import, init, initrd, iso, kernel, list, passwd, push, rekey, replace-cert, run, show, unlock
  ze bgp            [offline] BGP protocol tools
    decode <hex> | decode - | decode pcap <file>, encode <route>, plugin
  ze cli            [daemon ] Interactive CLI for the running daemon
    -c <cmd> for single command
  ze completion     [offline] Shell completion scripts
    bash, zsh, fish, nushell
  ze config         [offline] Configuration editing, formatting, validation, and history
    activate, archive, cat, completion, deactivate, diff, dump, edit, fix, fmt, graph, history, import, list, migrate, rename, rollback, set, show, validate
  ze connect        [offline] Manage SSH credentials for remote ze daemons
    add <host> [--port] [--user], list, remove <host> [--port], default <host> [--port]
  ze data           [offline] Store keys and blob artifact management
    backup, restore, write, import, rm, list, cat, registered, check, repair, encode
  ze doctor         [offline] Check if this box is ready to run Ze
    config <file>, kernel-capabilities, --json
  ze env            [offline] Environment variable inspection
    list, get, registered
  ze exabgp         [offline] ExaBGP bridge tools
    plugin, migrate
  ze firewall       [offline] Firewall management
    show, apply
  ze init           [setup  ] Initialize a live store or appliance seed with SSH credentials
    --managed --force --yes --web-cert <address> --web-cert-name <name> --seed --from <source> --sha256 <hex>
  ze install        [setup  ] Install ze binary, systemd service, or provision remote devices
    disk, local, remote, systemd
  ze interface      [offline] Manage OS network interfaces
    addr, clear, create, delete, down, mac, migrate, mtu, neighbors, routes, scan, show, unit, up
  ze isis           [offline] Offline IS-IS wire tools
    decode [--pretty]
  ze l2tp           [offline] L2TP tools
    decode, show [--user] <query>, tunnel [--user] {id <id> | all}, session [--user] {id <id> | all}
  ze ospf           [offline] Offline OSPF wire tools
    decode [--pretty]
  ze passwd         [setup  ] Change stored SSH/HTTP passwords
  ze pipe           [offline] Apply pipe operators to stdin
    json [<option>], ndjson, table, text, yaml, raw, no-more, log, save <path>, match <text>, count, first <n>, last <n>, display <field>..., fill [<option>], resolve, origin
  ze schema         [offline] Schema discovery
    events, handlers, list, methods, protocol
  ze secret         [offline] Decode a $9$ secret to its plaintext, or encode a plaintext
    decode, encode
  ze signal         [daemon ] Send signals to the daemon via SSH
    reload, stop, restart, reboot, status, quit
  ze start          [setup  ] Start the Ze daemon from blob storage config
    --web <port>, --web-only, --insecure-web, --mcp <port>
  ze status         [daemon ] Check if daemon is running
  ze sysctl         [offline] Kernel sysctl helpers
  ze tacacs         [offline] TACACS+ client helpers
    show
  ze traffic        [offline] Linux tc / VPP policer helpers
    control
  ze uninstall      [setup  ] Remove ze binary or systemd service
    local, systemd
  ze version        [offline] Show the running Ze version and build date
    --extended
  ze yang           [offline] YANG tree analysis
    completion, doc, tree

## Daemon API Commands (YANG RPCs)

Format: wire-method (dispatch-key) description

  ze-bfd:show-profile                          (show bfd profile              ) Return resolved BFD profile parameters. [read-only]
    name                     Profile name (empty returns every profile).
  ze-bfd:show-session                          (show bfd session address      ) Return one BFD session by peer address. [read-only]
    peer                     Peer IPv4 or IPv6 address. (REQUIRED)
  ze-bfd:show-sessions                         (show bfd sessions             ) Return every live BFD session. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:announce-blackhole                    (send bgp blackhole            ) Announce a route on demand (unicast, blackhole, flowspec).
  ze-bgp:announce-flowspec                     (send bgp flowspec             ) Announce a route on demand (unicast, blackhole, flowspec).
  ze-bgp:announce-unicast                      (send bgp unicast              ) Announce a route on demand (unicast, blackhole, flowspec).
  ze-bgp:cache-list                            (show cache                    ) BGP message cache operations. [read-only]
    action                   Cache action (list|retain|release|expire|forward) (REQUIRED)
    message-id               Cache message ID
    peer-selector            Target peers (for forward)
  ze-bgp:commit                                (request commit                ) Named commit operations.
    name                     Commit name
  ze-bgp:monitor                               (monitor bgp                   ) Stream live BGP events with optional filters. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:overview                              (show bgp                      ) Show the BGP overview (peer table with statistics). [read-only]
  ze-bgp:peer-borr                             (request peer borr             ) Send Beginning of Route Refresh.
    peer-selector            Target peers (REQUIRED)
    family                   Address family (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-capabilities                     (show bgp peer capabilities    ) Show negotiated capabilities for peer. [read-only]
    selector                 Peer filter (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-clear-soft                       (request peer clear soft       ) Soft-clear peer (send ROUTE-REFRESH per negotiated family).
    selector                 Peer address (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-create                           (create bgp peer               ) Create a peer in the running daemon.
    address                  Peer address (REQUIRED)
    asn                      Peer ASN, in any notation RFC 5396 names (REQUIRED)
    local-as                 Local ASN override, in any notation RFC 5396 names
    local-address            Local bind address
    router-id                Router ID override
    receive-hold-time        Receive hold time (RFC 4271)
    send-hold-time           Send hold time (RFC 9687, 0=auto)
    connect-retry            Connect retry interval
    connect                  Dial the peer (default true)
    accept                   Answer a connection from the peer (default true)
    graceful-restart         Restart Time in seconds (RFC 4724)
    group-updates            Group this peer's UPDATEs with other peers (default true)
    attach                   Plugin process this peer feeds
    family                   Address family to negotiate
  ze-bgp:peer-delete                           (delete bgp peer               ) Delete a peer from the running daemon.
  ze-bgp:peer-detail                           (show bgp peer detail          ) Show detailed peer information. [read-only]
    selector                 Peer filter
  ze-bgp:peer-disable                          (request peer disable          ) Hold a peer administratively down.
    selector                 Peer filter (REQUIRED)
    message                  Shutdown communication
  ze-bgp:peer-enable                           (request peer enable           ) Release a peer's administrative hold.
    selector                 Peer filter (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-eorr                             (request peer eorr             ) Send End of Route Refresh.
    peer-selector            Target peers (REQUIRED)
    family                   Address family (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-flush                            (request peer flush            ) Wait for forward pool to drain (barrier).
    selector                 Peer filter (* for all) (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-list                             (show bgp peer list            ) List configured peers. [read-only]
    selector                 Peer filter
  ze-bgp:peer-notify                           (request peer notify           ) Close a peer session with a NOTIFICATION of any code and subcode.
    selector                 Peer filter (REQUIRED)
    code                     NOTIFICATION error code (REQUIRED)
    subcode                  NOTIFICATION error subcode (REQUIRED)
    hex                      Data field octets in hexadecimal
    text                     Data field text
  ze-bgp:peer-raw                              (send bgp raw                  ) Send raw bytes to peer (no validation).
    peer-selector            Target peers (REQUIRED)
    type                     Message type hint
    encoding                 Data encoding (REQUIRED)
    data                     Raw data (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:peer-refresh                          (request peer refresh          ) Send ROUTE-REFRESH to peer for specified family.
  ze-bgp:peer-save                             (update bgp config             ) Write the running peer set to the configuration file.
  ze-bgp:peer-statistics                       (show bgp peer statistics      ) Show per-peer update statistics with rates. [read-only]
    selector                 Peer filter
  ze-bgp:peer-teardown                         (request peer teardown         ) Teardown peer session with CEASE notification.
    selector                 Peer filter (REQUIRED)
    subcode                  CEASE subcode
  ze-bgp:peer-update                           (send bgp update               ) Batch UPDATE with text/hex/b64 encoding.
    peer-selector            Target peers (REQUIRED)
    encoding                 Command encoding (REQUIRED)
    command                  Route DSL command (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:plugin-session-peer-ready             (request peer plugin session ready) Signal that this peer's plugin process finished its initialization.
    session                  Initial-replay session token
  ze-bgp:rib-best                              (show bgp rib best             ) Show best-path per prefix (RFC 4271 §9.1.2). [read-only]
    peer                     Filter by peer
    args                     Pipeline args: filters, terminal
  ze-bgp:rib-best-status                       (show bgp rib best status      ) Show best-path computation status. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:rib-clear-advertised                  (clear bgp rib advertised      ) Withdraw the Adj-RIB-Out of the selected peers.
    selector                 Peer filter (* for all) (REQUIRED)
    family                   Address family
  ze-bgp:rib-clear-in                          (clear bgp rib in              ) Clear Adj-RIB-In entries.
    peer                     Filter by peer
    family                   Filter by address family
  ze-bgp:rib-clear-out                         (clear bgp rib out             ) Resend the Adj-RIB-Out routes to the matching peers.
    peer                     Filter by peer
    family                   Filter by address family
  ze-bgp:rib-inject                            (request bgp rib inject        ) Insert route into Adj-RIB-In as if received from a peer.
    peer                     Peer address label (REQUIRED)
    family                   Address family (e.g. ipv4/unicast) (REQUIRED)
    prefix                   CIDR prefix (e.g. 10.0.0.0/24) (REQUIRED)
    origin                   Origin: igp, egp, incomplete (default: igp)
    nhop                     Next-hop IP address
    nexthop                  Alias for nhop next-hop IP address
    aspath                   AS path as comma-separated ASNs (e.g. 64500,64501)
    localpref                LOCAL_PREF value
    med                      MULTI_EXIT_DISC value
  ze-bgp:rib-routes                            (show bgp rib                  ) Show routes with pipeline filters. [read-only]
    peer                     Filter by peer
    args                     Pipeline args: scope, filters, terminal
  ze-bgp:rib-status                            (show bgp rib status           ) RIB summary: peer count, route counts, GR state. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:rib-withdraw                          (request bgp rib withdraw      ) Remove route from Adj-RIB-In.
    peer                     Peer address label (REQUIRED)
    family                   Address family (REQUIRED)
    prefix                   CIDR prefix to withdraw (REQUIRED)
  ze-bgp:show-announcements                    (show announcements            ) List active on-demand announcements. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:show-health                           (show bgp health               ) Show BGP peer health sorted by state and activity. [read-only]
  ze-bgp:withdraw-all                          (send bgp withdraw all         ) Withdraw on-demand announcements (by tag, id, or all).
  ze-bgp:withdraw-id                           (send bgp withdraw id          ) Withdraw on-demand announcements (by tag, id, or all).
  ze-bgp:withdraw-tag                          (send bgp withdraw tag         ) Withdraw on-demand announcements (by tag, id, or all).
  ze-cmd:bgp-metrics-list                      (show metrics list             ) List metric names only. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:bgp-metrics-values                    (show metrics values           ) Show Prometheus metrics in text format. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:bgp-subscribe                         (request subscribe             ) Subscribe to BGP events (streaming).
    events                   Event types to subscribe to
  ze-cmd:bgp-unsubscribe                       (request unsubscribe           ) Unsubscribe from BGP events.
  ze-cmd:show-event-delivery                   (show event delivery           ) Show which peers feed which attached processes. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:show-event-namespaces                 (show event namespaces         ) Show registered event namespaces with counts. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:show-event-recent                     (show event recent             ) Show recent events from global event ring. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:show-health                           (show health                   ) Show aggregated component health status. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:show-metrics-query                    (show metrics name             ) Query Prometheus metrics by name and label filter. [read-only]
  ze-cmd:show-warnings                         (show warnings                 ) Show active prefix warnings (stale data, threshold exceeded). [read-only]
  ze-config:archive-trigger                    (request config archive        ) Trigger a named config archive destination.
  ze-diag:show-capture                         (show capture                  ) Show captured control messages. [read-only]
  ze-iface:clear-interface-counters            (clear interface counters all  ) Reset RX/TX counters on one or all interfaces.
  ze-iface:interface-addr-add                  (create interface address      ) Add an IP address to an interface.
    name                     Interface name (REQUIRED)
    prefix                   IP address in CIDR notation (e.g. 10.0.0.1/24) (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-addr-del                  (delete interface name address ) Remove an IP address from an interface.
    name                     Interface name (REQUIRED)
    prefix                   IP address in CIDR notation (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-create-dummy              (create interface dummy name   ) Create a dummy (loopback-like) interface.
    name                     Interface name (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-create-veth               (create interface veth name    ) Create a veth pair.
    name                     Interface name (REQUIRED)
    peer                     Peer interface name (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-delete                    (delete interface name         ) Delete an interface.
    name                     Interface name (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-migrate                   (request interface migrate     ) Make-before-break IP migration between interfaces.
    from                     Source interface.unit (e.g. eth0.0) (REQUIRED)
    to                       Destination interface.unit (e.g. eth1.0) (REQUIRED)
    address                  IP address to migrate (CIDR) (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-unit-add                  (create interface bridge name unit) Add a VLAN logical unit to an interface.
    name                     Parent interface name (REQUIRED)
    vid                      VLAN ID (1-4094) (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:interface-unit-del                  (delete interface name unit    ) Delete a logical unit from an interface.
    name                     Parent interface name (REQUIRED)
    vid                      VLAN ID (1-4094) (REQUIRED)
  ze-iface:show-route-lookup                   (show route lookup             ) Longest-prefix-match route lookup for a destination IP. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:config                               (show l2tp config              ) Return effective runtime configuration. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:cqm                                  (show l2tp cqm                 ) Return per-login CQM bucket history. [read-only]
    login                    Login name, or 'summary' for aggregate view.
  ze-l2tp:echo                                 (show l2tp echo                ) Return the current echo state of one login. [read-only]
    login                    Login name. (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:listeners                            (show l2tp listeners           ) List bound UDP listener endpoints. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:observer                             (show l2tp observer            ) Return per-session event ring snapshot. [read-only]
    session-id               Local session ID (1..65535), or omit for 'all'.
  ze-l2tp:outgoing-call                        (request l2tp outgoing-call remote called) Place an LNS-side outgoing call toward a configured remote (RFC 2661 Section 10.4).
    remote                   Name of a configured l2tp/remote dial target. (REQUIRED)
    called                   Called Number placed in the OCRQ (RFC 2661 Section 7.9). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:pppoe-interfaces                     (show pppoe interfaces         ) List configured PPPoE access interfaces. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:pppoe-session                        (show pppoe session id         ) Return one session by session ID. [read-only]
    session-id               PPPoE session ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:pppoe-sessions                       (show pppoe sessions           ) List every live PPPoE session across all interfaces. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:pppoe-statistics                     (show pppoe statistics         ) Return protocol counters: active sessions per interface, discovery packet counts. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:pppoe-summary                        (show pppoe                    ) Return subsystem summary: session count, interface count, aggregate state. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:reliable                             (show l2tp reliable            ) Return the reliable transport window state of one tunnel. [read-only]
    tunnel-id                Local tunnel ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:session                              (show l2tp session id          ) Return one session by local session ID. [read-only]
    session-id               Local session ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:session-history                      (show l2tp session history     ) Return FSM transition history for a session. [read-only]
    session-id               Local session ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:session-teardown                     (clear l2tp session id         ) Send CDN Result Code 3 (administrative) for the session with the given local session ID.
    session-id               Local session ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:session-teardown-all                 (clear l2tp session all        ) Stop every live session on every tunnel on every listener.
  ze-l2tp:sessions                             (show l2tp sessions            ) List every live session across all tunnels. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:show-health                          (show l2tp health              ) Show L2TP session health sorted by echo loss. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:statistics                           (show l2tp statistics          ) Return the L2TP protocol counters. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:summary                              (show l2tp                     ) Return subsystem summary: tunnel count, session count, listener count, aggregate state. [read-only]
  ze-l2tp:tunnel                               (show l2tp tunnel id           ) Return one tunnel by local tunnel ID. [read-only]
    tunnel-id                Local tunnel ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:tunnel-history                       (show l2tp tunnel history      ) Return FSM transition history for a tunnel. [read-only]
    tunnel-id                Local tunnel ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:tunnel-teardown                      (clear l2tp tunnel id          ) Send StopCCN Result Code 6 (administrative) for the tunnel with the given local tunnel ID.
    tunnel-id                Local tunnel ID (1..65535). (REQUIRED)
  ze-l2tp:tunnel-teardown-all                  (clear l2tp tunnel all         ) Send StopCCN Result Code 6 (administrative) for every live tunnel on every listener.
  ze-l2tp:tunnels                              (show l2tp tunnels             ) List every live tunnel. [read-only]
  ze-log:bgp-log-levels                        (show log levels               ) Show current log levels for all subsystems. [read-only]
  ze-log:bgp-log-recent                        (show log recent               ) Show recent log entries from ring buffer with optional level/component/count filters. [read-only]
  ze-log:bgp-log-set                           (request log level             ) Set log level for a subsystem at runtime.
  ze-meta:bgp-command-complete                 (show command complete         ) Complete BGP command/args. [read-only]
    partial                  Partial command string (REQUIRED)
  ze-meta:bgp-command-help                     (show command help             ) Show BGP command details. [read-only]
    name                     Command name (REQUIRED)
  ze-meta:bgp-command-list                     (show command list             ) List BGP commands. [read-only]
  ze-meta:bgp-event-list                       (show event list               ) List available event types. [read-only]
  ze-meta:bgp-help                             (help                          ) List BGP subcommands. [read-only]
  ze-meta:bgp-plugin-ack                       (plugin ack                    ) Set ACK timing (sync|async). [read-only]
    mode                     ACK mode (REQUIRED)
  ze-meta:bgp-plugin-encoding                  (plugin encoding               ) Set event encoding (json|text). [read-only]
    encoding                 Encoding format (REQUIRED)
  ze-meta:bgp-plugin-format                    (plugin format                 ) Set wire format (hex|base64|parsed|full). [read-only]
    format                   Wire format (REQUIRED)
  ze-meta:event-monitor                        (monitor event                 ) Stream live BGP events with optional filters. [read-only]
  ze-ping:show-ping                            (show ping                     ) ICMP ping from the router to a destination IP. [read-only]
  ze-pki:show-certificate                      (show pki certificate name     ) Show details, PEM, bundle, or fingerprint of a named certificate. [read-only]
    name                     Certificate name to look up.
  ze-pki:show-certificates                     (show pki certificates         ) List all loaded certificates (CA and device). [read-only]
  ze-plugin:command-complete                   (plugin command complete       ) List the completion candidates for a partial plugin command. [read-only]
    partial                  Partial command string (REQUIRED)
  ze-plugin:command-help                       (plugin command help           ) Show one plugin command's summary, explanation, arguments, and source plugin. [read-only]
    name                     Command name (REQUIRED)
  ze-plugin:command-list                       (plugin command list           ) List every command a plugin registered, with its summary. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:help                               (plugin help                   ) List the subcommands the plugin verb accepts. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:session-bye                        (plugin session bye            ) Tell the daemon this session is disconnecting. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:session-ping                       (plugin session ping           ) Answer a health check with the daemon process id. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:session-ready                      (plugin session ready          ) Signal that this plugin process finished its initialization. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-command-complete            (system command complete       ) List the completion candidates for a partial command. [read-only]
    partial                  Partial command string (REQUIRED)
    arg                      Current argument being completed
  ze-plugin:system-command-help                (system command help           ) Show the detailed help for one command. [read-only]
    name                     Command name (REQUIRED)
  ze-plugin:system-command-list                (system command list           ) List every command the daemon knows. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-daemon-quit                 (request halt                  ) Dump every goroutine stack, then shut the daemon down.
  ze-plugin:system-daemon-reboot               (request reboot                ) Shut the daemon down gracefully, then reboot the system (root is required on Linux).
  ze-plugin:system-daemon-reload               (request reload                ) Reload the configuration.
  ze-plugin:system-daemon-shutdown             (request shutdown              ) Shut the daemon down gracefully.
  ze-plugin:system-daemon-status               (show status                   ) Show the daemon uptime, peer count, and start time. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-dispatch                    (system dispatch               ) Dispatch a text command through the command dispatcher. [read-only]
    args                     Command words to join and dispatch
  ze-plugin:system-help                        (system help                   ) List the subcommands the system verb accepts. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-quiesce                     (request quiesce               ) Block until every subsystem drains its pending async work.
  ze-plugin:system-subsystem-list              (system subsystem list         ) List the subsystems registered in the daemon. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-version-api                 (system version api            ) Show the IPC protocol version. [read-only]
  ze-plugin:system-version-software            (system version software       ) Show the ze software version. [read-only]
  ze-resolve:clear-dns-cache                   (clear dns cache all           ) Flush DNS cache entries or reset cache counters.
  ze-resolve:cymru-asn-name                    (resolve cymru asn-name        ) Look up organization name for an ASN via Team Cymru DNS. [read-only]
    asn                      Autonomous System Number (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:dns-a                             (resolve dns a                 ) Resolve DNS A records (IPv4 addresses). [read-only]
    name                     Hostname to resolve (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:dns-aaaa                          (resolve dns aaaa              ) Resolve DNS AAAA records (IPv6 addresses). [read-only]
    name                     Hostname to resolve (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:dns-ptr                           (resolve dns ptr               ) Reverse DNS lookup (PTR records). [read-only]
    address                  IP address for reverse lookup (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:dns-txt                           (resolve dns txt               ) Resolve DNS TXT records. [read-only]
    name                     Hostname to resolve (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:irr-expand                        (resolve irr expand            ) Recursively expand AS-SET to member ASNs. [read-only]
    as-set                   AS-SET name (e.g. AS-CLOUDFLARE) (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:irr-prefix                        (resolve irr prefix            ) Look up prefixes for an AS-SET from IRR. [read-only]
    as-set                   AS-SET name (e.g. AS-CLOUDFLARE) (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:peeringdb-as-set                  (resolve peeringdb as-set      ) Look up AS-SET names for an ASN from PeeringDB. [read-only]
    asn                      Autonomous System Number (REQUIRED)
  ze-resolve:peeringdb-max-prefix              (resolve peeringdb max-prefix  ) Look up maximum prefix counts for an ASN from PeeringDB. [read-only]
    asn                      Autonomous System Number (REQUIRED)
  ze-test-fakeas112:emit                       (fakeas112 emit                ) Emit the AS112 covering prefixes as one route-change batch per family.
