  firewall-irr             IRR-based prefix-list filtering for firewall rules
  flow-export              sFlow, NetFlow v9, and IPFIX counter export
  flowspec-firewall        Translates BGP FlowSpec routes into nftables firewall rules
  geodns                   GeoDNS server: DNS answers selected by client source IP (RFC 1035, RFC 7871 client-subnet)
  ike                      IKEv2 engine for native IPsec VPN
  imageserver              Image server: HTTP provisioning for disk images and boot files
  interface                OS network interface monitoring and management
  isis                     Intermediate System to Intermediate System (ISO/IEC 10589, RFC 1195): native link-state IGP
    RFCs: 1195, 5301, 5303, 5305, 5308, 5310
  kernel                   Kernel routes: redistribute externally-installed kernel routes into BGP
  l2tp-auth-local          Static local user list for L2TP PPP authentication
  l2tp-auth-radius         RADIUS authentication and accounting for L2TP PPP sessions
  l2tp-pool                IPv4 address and IPv6 prefix pool for L2TP PPP sessions
  l2tp-shaper              Traffic shaping for L2TP subscriber sessions
  ldp                      Label Distribution Protocol (RFC 5036): MPLS label distribution
  loop                     Route loop detection (RFC 4271 S9, RFC 4456 S8)
    RFCs: 4271, 4456
  mrt                      MRT routing information export (RFC 6396)
  ntp                      NTP client: system clock synchronization
  ospf                     Open Shortest Path First v2 (RFC 2328): native link-state IPv4 IGP
    RFCs: 2328, 5709, 7474, 9129
  policy                   Route policy library: the policy root, named filter instances and the route field vocabulary
  policy-routes            Policy-based routing: nftables packet marking and ip rule table selection
  redistribute-orchestrator Redistribute orchestrator: dispatches protocol route events to registered consumers
  rib                      System RIB: selects best route across protocols by admin distance
  routing-table            Named routing table registry: maps names to kernel table IDs
  rsvp-te                  RSVP-TE: Resource Reservation Protocol - Traffic Engineering (RFC 3209)
  static                   Static routes: config-driven kernel/VPP route programming with ECMP
  sysctl                   Kernel tunable management: three-layer precedence, restore on stop
  tftpserver               TFTP server: read-only file serving for PXE boot (RFC 1350, RFC 2347 option negotiation)
  traffic                  Traffic control (tc) qdisc, class, and filter management
  traffic-usage            eBPF TCX per-port and per-IP byte accounting
  vpp                      VPP data plane lifecycle management
  vrrp                     Virtual Router Redundancy Protocol (RFC 9568 / RFC 3768): first-hop gateway redundancy
    RFCs: 9568, 3768

## Peer Selectors

  Most commands accept a peer selector to target specific peers.
  The reactor resolves selectors in priority order:

  *                All peers (default when omitted)
  192.168.1.1      Exact IP address
  my-peer          Peer name (from config, takes priority over IP)
  as65001          All peers with remote AS 65001 (case-insensitive)
  10.0.0.*         IP glob pattern (per-octet wildcard)
  !192.168.1.1     Exclusion: all peers except this one
  10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2  Comma-separated list (RIB commands only)

## Family-Specific Attributes

  Some update text attributes only apply to specific address families:

  path-id <N>        ADD-PATH peers only (any family, requires ADD-PATH capability)
  rd <value>         VPN families: ipv4/mpls-vpn, ipv6/mpls-vpn, l2vpn/evpn, l2vpn/vpls
  label <N>          Labeled/VPN: ipv4/mpls-label, ipv6/mpls-label, */vpn

## RIB Show Pipeline

  show bgp rib [scope] [filters...] [terminal]
  show bgp rib best [filters...] [terminal]

  Scopes (positional, first argument):
    received         Adj-RIB-In only
    sent             Adj-RIB-Out only
    sent-received    Both (default)

  Filters (named, chainable):
    family <afi/safi>     Address family (e.g. ipv4/unicast)
    prefix <pattern>      Prefix string match (e.g. 192.168)
    path <pattern>        AS-path: 64501 (anywhere), ^64501 (anchored), 64501,64502 (contiguous)
    community <value>     Exact community match (e.g. 65000:100)
    match <text>          Case-insensitive substring across all fields

  Terminals (last argument):
    count                 Return {"count": N} instead of routes
    json                  Full route details (default)

  Examples:
    show bgp rib received family ipv4/unicast
    show bgp rib sent prefix 10.0 count
    show bgp rib received community 65000:100 path ^64501
    show bgp rib best family ipv4/unicast json

