## MCP Tools (via --mcp <port>)

  Start: ze start --mcp <port> <config>  or  ze --mcp <port> -
  Connect: POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp with a JSON-RPC body

  Protocol revision 2026-07-28 (the only one accepted). Stateless: every
  message is its own POST, with no initialize handshake and no session.

  Required on every POST:
    MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28   header, must match the _meta version
    Mcp-Method: <method>               header, must match the body's method
    Mcp-Name: <params.name>            header, tools/call + prompts/get
    Mcp-Name: <params.uri>             header, resources/read
    params._meta["io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion"]    (required)
    params._meta["io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities"] (required, {} is valid)

  Tools are auto-generated from the YANG command registry at tools/list time.
  Each command group becomes a tool with an action enum. New YANG commands
  appear as MCP tools automatically.

  Handcrafted tools:
  ze_execute          Run any Ze command (escape hatch)
    command           Full command string (REQUIRED)

  ze_reference        Full AI reference for this daemon (same as 'ze help ai --json')

  Call server/discover first to learn the supported versions and capabilities,
  then tools/list against a live daemon for the full tool inventory.

  JSON-RPC Example (headers shown above are required and not repeated here):
    {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"ze_execute",
     "arguments":{"command":"summary"},
     "_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28",
              "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}

  Every successful result carries resultType:"complete" and
  _meta["io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo"].

## Services (from YANG environment containers)

  Optional services started alongside the BGP daemon.
  Enable via config block or CLI flag. Web UI requires ze init (blob storage).

  api-server: API engine settings (shared parent for the REST/gRPC transports)
    Config:    environment { api-server { } }
    token                Bearer token for API authentication.
    Env vars:  ze.api-server.grpc.enabled, ze.api-server.grpc.listen, ze.api-server.rest.enabled, ze.api-server.rest.listen, ze.api-server.token

  api-server: API engine settings (shared parent; merged across modules)
    Config:    environment { api-server { } }
    grpc                 gRPC API transport. Authenticated non-loopback listeners
require tls-cert and tls-key.
    Env vars:  ze.api-server.grpc.enabled, ze.api-server.grpc.listen, ze.api-server.rest.enabled, ze.api-server.rest.listen, ze.api-server.token

  api-server: API engine settings (shared parent; merged across modules)
    Config:    environment { api-server { } }
    rest                 REST and HTTP transport for the API server.
    Env vars:  ze.api-server.grpc.enabled, ze.api-server.grpc.listen, ze.api-server.rest.enabled, ze.api-server.rest.listen, ze.api-server.token

  bgp: BGP protocol environment settings, applied before any peer-level config.
    Config:    environment { bgp { announce-delay 0s; openwait 120; } }
    announce-delay       Delay between reactor Ready and first UPDATE (duration, 0s-1h) (default: 0s)
    openwait             Seconds to wait for peer OPEN after TCP connect (default: 120)
    Env vars:  ze.bgp.announce.delay, ze.bgp.chaos.rate, ze.bgp.chaos.seed, ze.bgp.openwait, ze.bgp.reactor.cache-max, ze.bgp.reactor.cache-ttl, ze.bgp.reactor.coalesce, ze.bgp.reactor.forward-dedup, ze.bgp.reactor.speed, ze.bgp.reactor.update-groups, ze.bgp.rib.bestprev.shards, ze.bgp.route-server.worker-queue-size

  bmp: BMP receiver settings
    Config:    environment { bmp { enabled false; max-sessions 100; route-action monitor; } }
    enabled              Enable BMP receiver (default: false)
    max-sessions         Maximum concurrent BMP sessions (default: 100)
    route-action         Action for received BMP Route Monitoring messages (default: monitor)
    server               BMP receiver listen endpoints

  chaos: Chaos fault injection settings
    Config:    environment { chaos { rate 0.1; } }
    rate                 Fault probability per operation (0.0-1.0) (default: 0.1)
    seed                 PRNG seed (0 = disabled)

  cli: CLI session settings
    Config:    environment { cli { transcript disabled; } }
    format               Default output format settings
    transcript           CLI session transcript recording to $XDG_DATA_HOME/ze/transcripts/ (default: disabled)
    Env vars:  ze.cli.format, ze.cli.transcript

  daemon: Daemon settings
    Config:    environment { daemon { user zeuser; } }
    pid                  PID file path
    user                 System user for privilege drop (default: zeuser)

  exabgp: ExaBGP compatibility settings for the migration bridge
    Config:    environment { exabgp { } }
    api                  ExaBGP bridge API settings

  gnmi: Settings of the gNMI server.
    Config:    environment { gnmi { enabled false; } }
    enabled              Start the gNMI server. (default: false)
    server               Listen endpoints of the gNMI server.
    tls                  TLS certificate of the gNMI gRPC transport.
    token                Bearer token that authenticates a gNMI client.
    Env vars:  ze.gnmi.enabled, ze.gnmi.listen, ze.gnmi.tls.cert, ze.gnmi.tls.key, ze.gnmi.token

  l2tp: L2TP listener endpoints
    Config:    environment { l2tp { } }
    server               L2TP server listen endpoints (UDP)
    Env vars:  ze.l2tp.cqm.echo-interval, ze.l2tp.metrics.poll-interval

  log: Logging settings
    Config:    environment { log { destination stdout; level INFO; } }
    backend              Log output backend (default: stderr)
    color                Force color log output on (true) or off (false). When unset, auto-detected from terminal.
    destination          Syslog address used when backend is syslog: empty, a socket path, or host:port (default: stdout)
    level                Base log level for all subsystems: disabled, debug, info, warn, or err (case-insensitive) (default: INFO)
    relay                Plugin stderr relay level: disabled, debug, info, warn, or err (case-insensitive)
    Env vars:  ze.log, ze.log.backend, ze.log.color, ze.log.destination, ze.log.relay

  looking-glass: Looking glass HTTP server settings.
    Config:    environment { looking-glass { enabled false; tls true; } }
    certificate          PKI store certificate served on the looking-glass listener (ze.looking-glass.certificate).
    enabled              Enable the looking glass. (default: false)
    server               Looking glass listen endpoints.
    tls                  Enable TLS. Override with the ze.looking-glass.tls variable. (default: true)
    token                Bearer token checked on every /api/ and /lg/ route (ze.looking-glass.token).
    Env vars:  ze.looking-glass.certificate, ze.looking-glass.enabled, ze.looking-glass.listen, ze.looking-glass.tls, ze.looking-glass.token

  mcp: Settings of the MCP server.
    CLI flag:  --mcp <port>
    Config:    environment { mcp { bind-remote false; enabled false; } }
    auth-mode            Authentication strategy for the MCP server.
    bind-remote          Allow the MCP server to bind to a non-loopback address. (default: false)
    enabled              Start the MCP server. (default: false)
    identity             Per-identity bearer entries, for auth-mode=bearer-list.
    oauth                OAuth 2.1 resource-server settings, for auth-mode=oauth.
    server               Listen endpoints of the MCP server.
    tls                  TLS certificate that serves the MCP endpoint over HTTPS.
    token                Bearer token for auth-mode=bearer.
    Env vars:  ze.mcp.auth-mode, ze.mcp.bind-remote, ze.mcp.enabled, ze.mcp.listen, ze.mcp.oauth.audience, ze.mcp.oauth.authorization-server, ze.mcp.oauth.required-scopes, ze.mcp.tls.cert, ze.mcp.tls.key, ze.mcp.token

  mtu: Settings of the path MTU diagnostic.
    Config:    environment { mtu { } }
    reference-address    Address show mtu measures to tell a clamped circuit from a clamped peer path.
    Env vars:  ze.mtu.reference-address

  ntp: Settings of the NTP client.
    Config:    environment { ntp { enabled false; interval 3600; max-step 3600; persist-path /perm/ze/timefile; slew-threshold 128; } }
    enabled              Synchronize the system clock with an NTP server. (default: false)
    interval             Seconds between two clock synchronizations. (default: 3600)
    max-step             Largest clock step in seconds that Ze accepts. (default: 3600)
    persist-path         Path of the file that holds the time across a restart. (default: /perm/ze/timefile)
    server               The NTP servers Ze queries.
    slew-threshold       Maximum offset in milliseconds for a gradual clock slew. (default: 128)

  reactor: BGP reactor engine tuning.
    Config:    environment { reactor { cache-max 1000000; cache-ttl 60; forward-batch-limit 1024; forward-pool-headroom 0; forward-pool-max-bytes 0; forward-queue-size 256; forward-teardown-grace 5s; read-buffer-size 65536; speed 1.0; update-groups true; write-buffer-size 16384; } }
    cache-max            Maximum number of cached UPDATE wire messages. (default: 1000000)
    cache-ttl            Seconds Ze keeps a built UPDATE wire message in the encoding cache. (default: 60)
    forward-batch-limit  Max items per drain batch. Bounds writeMu hold time during forward dispatch. 0 means unlimited. (default: 1024)
    forward-pool-headroom Extra bytes beyond the auto-sized pool baseline. (default: 0)
    forward-pool-max-bytes Combined byte budget for the 4K and 64K buffer pools, in bytes. (default: 0)
    forward-queue-size   Per-destination forward channel capacity. (default: 256)
    forward-teardown-grace Grace period before forced teardown on congestion (duration string, e.g. 5s, 1m). (default: 5s)
    read-buffer-size     Per-session TCP read buffer size in bytes. (default: 65536)
    speed                Reactor loop cycle time multiplier, from 0.1 to 10.0. (default: 1.0)
    update-groups        Build each UPDATE once for every peer with the same encoding context. (default: true)
    write-buffer-size    Per-session TCP write buffer size in bytes. (default: 16384)

  ssh: SSH server settings.
    Config:    environment { ssh { enabled false; } }
    enabled              Enable the SSH server. (default: false)
    host-certificate     Path to the SSH host certificate file, signed by a CA.
    host-key             Path to the SSH host key file.
    idle-timeout         Idle timeout in seconds. The default is 600.
    max-sessions         Maximum number of concurrent SSH sessions.
    server               SSH server listen endpoints.
    Env vars:  ze.ssh.ephemeral, ze.ssh.host, ze.ssh.insecure, ze.ssh.password, ze.ssh.port, ze.ssh.username

  web: Web interface settings.
    CLI flag:  --web <port>  --web-only  --insecure-web
    Config:    environment { web { enabled false; insecure false; ui-mode finder; } }
    certificate          Name of the PKI store certificate served on the HTTPS listener (ze.web.certificate).
    enabled              Enable the web interface. (default: false)
    insecure             Disable authentication, which forces the host to 127.0.0.1. (default: false)
    server               Web server listen endpoints.
    ui-mode              Web UI mode. (default: finder)
    Env vars:  ze.web.certificate, ze.web.enabled, ze.web.insecure, ze.web.listen, ze.web.ui-mode

## Recipes

  Start daemon with MCP:
    ze init && ze start --mcp 9718

  Start with config file:
    ze config validate example.conf && ze --mcp 9718 example.conf

  Announce a route (CLI):
    ze cli -c "send bgp * update text origin igp next-hop 1.1.1.1 nlri add 10.0.0.0/24"

  Announce a route (MCP; POST to /mcp with the headers from the MCP Tools section):
    {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"ze_announce",
     "arguments":{"family":"ipv4/unicast","origin":"igp","next-hop":"1.1.1.1","prefixes":["10.0.0.0/24"]},
     "_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion":"2026-07-28",
              "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities":{}}}}

  Check peer state:
    ze cli -c "show bgp peer list"
    ze cli -c "show bgp peer test-peer detail"

  Show RIB:
    ze cli -c "show bgp rib received family ipv4/unicast"
    ze cli -c "show bgp rib best"

  Monitor live events:
    ze cli -c "bgp monitor"

  Drain and teardown a peer:
    ze cli -c "request peer 10.0.0.1 pause"
    ze cli -c "request peer * flush"
    ze cli -c "request peer 10.0.0.1 teardown"

  Test without a real peer:
    le test peer --mode sink --port 1179 --asn 65001

## Common Errors

  unknown family "ipv4-unicast"       Use slash separator: ipv4/unicast
  peer not found "10.0.0.1"           Peer not configured; check: peer list
  database already exists              Run: ze init --force (backs up old database)
  connection refused (SSH)             Daemon not running; start with: ze start
  no prefixes specified                REQUIRED field missing in ze_announce/ze_withdraw
  unknown command "..."                Use: ze_reference (MCP) or ze cli -c "help"
  web server disabled: persistent store unavailable  Run: ze init (creates the database/ store with TLS certs)

## Minimal Config

  bgp {
      router-id 10.0.0.1
      local {
          as 65000
      }
      peer test-peer {
          remote {
              ip 10.0.0.2
              as 65001
          }
          local {
              ip 10.0.0.1
          }
          family {
              ipv4/unicast
          }
      }
  }

  Validate: ze config validate <file>
  Start:    ze <file>  or  ze start (from database)

